1
00:00:00,712 --> 00:00:01,922
(Raj:)Hold on. We do that all the time.

2
00:00:02,081 --> 00:00:03,921
(Raj:)You and I work together
and play together.

3
00:00:04,049 --> 00:00:07,429
(Howard:)I know, and it drove me
into the arms of another woman.

4
00:00:09,521 --> 00:00:11,431
(Howard:)Bipolar Bear.

5
00:00:12,591 --> 00:00:14,431
(Sheldon:)Well, I appreciate your concern,

6
00:00:14,593 --> 00:00:17,233
(Sheldon:)but I won't be seeing any more of Amy
than I already do.

7
00:00:17,396 --> 00:00:19,706
(Sheldon:)I assume we'll deduct any extra time
we spend together

8
00:00:19,865 --> 00:00:22,245
(Sheldon:)at work from our weekly quota.

9
00:00:24,536 --> 00:00:27,206
(Leonard:)Please let me be there
when you tell her that.

10
00:00:28,307 --> 00:00:29,947
(Sheldon:)Why? So you can see the look
on Amy's face

11
00:00:30,042 --> 00:00:32,782
(Sheldon:)when she hears my top-notch idea?

12
00:00:32,878 --> 00:00:35,118
(Leonard:)Please, oh please,
just let me be there.

13
00:00:37,816 --> 00:00:40,316
(Bernadette:)So, Amy, what are you gonna be
working on at Caltech?

14
00:00:40,452 --> 00:00:41,932
(Amy:)I'm leading a study to see

15
00:00:42,087 --> 00:00:43,997
(Amy:)if deficiency of the monoamine
oxidase enzyme leads

16
00:00:44,156 --> 00:00:46,996
(Amy:)to paralyzing fear in monkeys.

17
00:00:47,126 --> 00:00:49,766
(Bernadette:)If they're anything like humans,
the answer's yes.

18
00:00:49,928 --> 00:00:52,308
Wait, you've done this
experiment on humans?

19
00:00:52,431 --> 00:00:55,101
(Bernadette:)You mean like death row inmates
with nothing to lose?

20
00:00:55,234 --> 00:00:59,024
(Bernadette:)No, that would be unethical.

